  /// was obtained on, the timestamp relevant to detection results and pointer to
  /// error message in case of any failure. The validity of the passed arguments
  /// is true for the lifetime of the callback function.
  ///
  /// The passed arguments are only valid for the lifetime of the callback.
  external ffi.Pointer<
    ffi.NativeFunction<
      ffi.Void Function(
        ffi.UnsignedInt status,
        ffi.Pointer<MpObjectDetectorResult> result,
        MpImagePtr image,
        ffi.Int64 timestamp_ms,
      )
    >
  >
  result_callback;
}

typedef MpObjectDetectorPtr = ffi.Pointer<MpObjectDetectorInternal>;
typedef MpObjectDetectorResult = MpDetectionResult;

final class MpPoseLandmarkerInternal extends ffi.Opaque {}

/// The options for configuring a MediaPipe pose landmarker task.
final class MpPoseLandmarkerOptions extends ffi.Struct {
  /// Base options for configuring MediaPipe Tasks, such as specifying the model
  /// file with metadata, accelerator options, op resolver, etc.
  external MpBaseOptions base_options;

  /// The running mode of the task. Default to the image mode.
  /// PoseLandmarker has three running modes:
  /// 1) The image mode for recognizing pose landmarks on single image inputs.
  /// 2) The video mode for recognizing pose landmarks on the decoded frames of a
  /// video.
  /// 3) The live stream mode for recognizing pose landmarks on the live stream
  /// of input data, such as from camera. In this mode, the "result_callback"
  /// below must be specified to receive the detection results asynchronously.
  @ffi.UnsignedInt()
  external int running_modeAsInt;

  MpRunningMode get running_mode => MpRunningMode.fromValue(running_modeAsInt);
  set running_mode(MpRunningMode value) => running_modeAsInt = value.value;

  /// The maximum number of poses can be detected by the PoseLandmarker.
  @ffi.Int()
  external int num_poses;

  /// The minimum confidence score for the pose detection to be considered
  /// successful.
  @ffi.Float()
  external double min_pose_detection_confidence;

  /// The minimum confidence score of pose presence score in the pose landmark
  /// detection.
  @ffi.Float()
  external double min_pose_presence_confidence;

  /// The minimum confidence score for the pose tracking to be considered
  /// successful.
  @ffi.Float()
  external double min_tracking_confidence;

  /// Whether to output segmentation masks.
  @ffi.Bool()
  external bool output_segmentation_masks;

  /// The user-defined result callback for processing live stream data.
  /// The result callback should only be specified when the running mode is set
  /// to MP_RUNNING_MODE_LIVE_STREAM. Arguments of the callback
  /// function include: the pointer to recognition result, the image that result
  /// was obtained on, the timestamp relevant to recognition results and pointer
  /// to error message in case of any failure. The validity of the passed
  /// arguments is true for the lifetime of the callback function.
  ///
  /// The passed arguments are only valid for the lifetime of the callback.
  external ffi.Pointer<
    ffi.NativeFunction<
      ffi.Void Function(
        ffi.UnsignedInt status,
        ffi.Pointer<MpPoseLandmarkerResult> result,
        MpImagePtr image,
        ffi.Int64 timestamp_ms,
      )
    >
  >
  result_callback;
}

typedef MpPoseLandmarkerPtr = ffi.Pointer<MpPoseLandmarkerInternal>;

/// The hand landmarker result from PoseLandmarker, where each vector
/// element represents a single hand detected in the image.
final class MpPoseLandmarkerResult extends ffi.Struct {
  /// Segmentation masks for pose.
  external ffi.Pointer<MpImagePtr> segmentation_masks;

  /// The number of elements in the segmentation_masks array.
  @ffi.Uint32()
  external int segmentation_masks_count;

  /// Detected hand landmarks in normalized image coordinates.
  external ffi.Pointer<MpNormalizedLandmarks> pose_landmarks;

  /// The number of elements in the pose_landmarks array.
  @ffi.Uint32()
  external int pose_landmarks_count;

  /// Detected hand landmarks in world coordinates.
  external ffi.Pointer<MpLandmarks> pose_world_landmarks;

  /// The number of elements in the pose_world_landmarks array.
  @ffi.Uint32()
  external int pose_world_landmarks_count;

  static ffi.Pointer<MpPoseLandmarkerResult> $allocate(
    ffi.Allocator $allocator, {
    required ffi.Pointer<MpImagePtr> segmentation_masks,
    required int segmentation_masks_count,
    required ffi.Pointer<MpNormalizedLandmarks> pose_landmarks,
    required int pose_landmarks_count,
    required ffi.Pointer<MpLandmarks> pose_world_landmarks,
    required int pose_world_landmarks_count,
  }) => $allocator<MpPoseLandmarkerResult>()
    ..ref.segmentation_masks = segmentation_masks
    ..ref.segmentation_masks_count = segmentation_masks_count
    ..ref.pose_landmarks = pose_landmarks
    ..ref.pose_landmarks_count = pose_landmarks_count
    ..ref.pose_world_landmarks = pose_world_landmarks
    ..ref.pose_world_landmarks_count = pose_world_landmarks_count;
}

/// Defines a rectangle, used e.g. as part of detection results or as input
/// region-of-interest.
final class MpRect extends ffi.Struct {
  @ffi.Int()
  external int left;

  @ffi.Int()
  external int top;

  @ffi.Int()
  external int bottom;

  @ffi.Int()
  external int right;

  static ffi.Pointer<MpRect> $allocate(
    ffi.Allocator $allocator, {
    required int left,
    required int top,
    required int bottom,
    required int right,
  }) => $allocator<MpRect>()
    ..ref.left = left
    ..ref.top = top
    ..ref.bottom = bottom
    ..ref.right = right;
}

/// The coordinates are normalized wrt the image dimensions, i.e. generally in
/// [0,1] but they may exceed these bounds if describing a region overlapping the
/// image. The origin is on the top-left corner of the image.
final class MpRectF extends ffi.Struct {
  @ffi.Float()
  external double left;

  @ffi.Float()
  external double top;

  @ffi.Float()
  external double bottom;

  @ffi.Float()
  external double right;

  static ffi.Pointer<MpRectF> $allocate(
    ffi.Allocator $allocator, {
    required double left,
    required double top,
    required double bottom,
    required double right,
  }) => $allocator<MpRectF>()
    ..ref.left = left
    ..ref.top = top
    ..ref.bottom = bottom
    ..ref.right = right;
}

/// The Region-Of-Interest (ROI) to interact with.
final class MpRegionOfInterest extends ffi.Struct {
  /// Specifies the format used to specify the region-of-interest. Note that
  /// using `MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED` is invalid.
  @ffi.UnsignedInt()
  external int formatAsInt;

  MpRegionOfInterestFormat get format => MpRegionOfInterestFormat.fromValue(formatAsInt);
  set format(MpRegionOfInterestFormat value) => formatAsInt = value.value;

  /// Represents the ROI in keypoint format, this should have a valid keypoint
  /// with coordinates `x` and `y` if `format` is
  /// `MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_KEYPOINT`; `nullptr` if not present
  external ffi.Pointer<MpNormalizedKeypoint> keypoint;

  /// Represents the ROI in scribble format, this should be not a `nullptr` if
  /// `format` is `MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_SCRIBBLE`; `nullptr` if not
  /// present
  external ffi.Pointer<MpNormalizedKeypoint> scribble;

  /// Number of keypoints in scribble; 0 if not present
  @ffi.Uint32()
  external int scribble_count;

  static ffi.Pointer<MpRegionOfInterest> $allocate(
    ffi.Allocator $allocator, {
    required MpRegionOfInterestFormat format,
    required ffi.Pointer<MpNormalizedKeypoint> keypoint,
    required ffi.Pointer<MpNormalizedKeypoint> scribble,
    required int scribble_count,
  }) => $allocator<MpRegionOfInterest>()
    ..ref.format = format
    ..ref.keypoint = keypoint
    ..ref.scribble = scribble
    ..ref.scribble_count = scribble_count;
}

/// The format used to specify the region-of-interest.
enum MpRegionOfInterestFormat {
  MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED(0),
  MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_KEYPOINT(1),
  MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_SCRIBBLE(2);

  final int value;
  const MpRegionOfInterestFormat(this.value);

  static MpRegionOfInterestFormat fromValue(int value) => switch (value) {
    0 => MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED,
    1 => MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_KEYPOINT,
    2 => MP_REGION_OF_INTEREST_FORMAT_SCRIBBLE,
    _ => throw ArgumentError('Unknown value for MpRegionOfInterestFormat: $value'),
  };
}

/// Supported processing modes.
enum MpRunningMode {
  MP_RUNNING_MODE_IMAGE(1),
  MP_RUNNING_MODE_VIDEO(2),
  MP_RUNNING_MODE_LIVE_STREAM(3);

  final int value;
  const MpRunningMode(this.value);

  static MpRunningMode fromValue(int value) => switch (value) {
    1 => MP_RUNNING_MODE_IMAGE,
    2 => MP_RUNNING_MODE_VIDEO,
    3 => MP_RUNNING_MODE_LIVE_STREAM,
    _ => throw ArgumentError('Unknown value for MpRunningMode: $value'),
  };
}

